    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "summary",
     "content_html": "<p>Convert the base 10 number into base 20.</p>\n<p>Step 1: Divide the number by 20.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"137 \\div 20 = 6\"></span> with a remainder. What is it?</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"20 \\times 6 = 120\"></span></p>\n<table class=\"unnumbered unstyled\">\n<tbody>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"137-120 = 17\"></span></td>\n<td><span data-math=\"6{\\rm{R}}17\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td>Step 2: Divide the quotient by 20.</td>\n<td></td>\n</tr>\n<tr>\n<td><span data-math=\"6 \\div 20 = 0\"></span> with remainder 6.</td>\n<td><span data-math=\"0{\\rm{R}}6\"></span></td>\n</tr>\n</tbody>\n</table>\n<p>The base 20 number has digits equal to the remainders in reverse order.</p>\n<p><span data-math=\"6 \\times {20^1} + 17 \\times {20^0}\"></span></p>\n<p>The Mayan number would have 6 in the top row and 17 in the bottom row.</p>\n<p>In the top row, the symbol would have one bar and one dot.</p>\n<p>In the bottom row, the symbol would have three bars and two dots.</p>"
    },
    {
     "images": [],
     "solution_type": "detailed",
     "content_html": "<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBc1VKIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--a54f02e1ca09c2d36f1dabb6f9adcb4347b10aa4/M17.jpg\" alt=\"Mayan numeral 17 is displayed.\"><br>\n<img src=\"https://exercises.openstax.org/rails/active_storage/blobs/proxy/eyJfcmFpbHMiOnsibWVzc2FnZSI6IkJBaHBBdHNPIiwiZXhwIjpudWxsLCJwdXIiOiJibG9iX2lkIn19--f6d8d2e74ee216a9290d496a2e084e241b33a6fa/M06.png\" alt=\"Mayan numeral 6 is displayed.\">"
    }
